# python environment and notebooks

The following scripts have been developed on xUbuntu 20.04.6 LTS on  PC with a NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 and CUDA Version: 12.2. Adaptations to the following code may be needed when using different versions of Linux distributions or hardware.

Copy all files in this repo e.g. to ~/Documents

Please read and try to understand the code for later troubleshooting.


# Create /use python 3.73 virtual environment with required packages

## Creation of python environment see:

https://github.com/neuropathbasel/nanodip_dependencies

## Activate the virtual environment:

source /applications/nanodipVenv01/bin/activate

cd /applications/nanodip

jupyter notebook

Copy NanoDiP_allinone_50_MSA.ipynb to

/applications/nanodip

on your local machine

In the jupyter notebook  open

NanoDiP_allinone_50_MSA.ipynb

And adjust it to your paths if required and save it as  NanoDiP_allinone_50_MSA.py

In xterm activate the virtual environment running

source /applications/nanodipVenv01/bin/activate

And start the nanodip server with

python3 NanoDiP_allinone_50_MSA.py

Open in a browser and address
http://localhost:8081/
(the correct port is given in the command line after starting the NanoDiP server.

In the resulting webpage navigate to EpidiP UMAP	

In both drop down menus select ND_IfP_20250912.xlsx and set the top n probes to 5000 and activate re-generate UMAP.
